;; Maturity loop for the yabai worldwide phishing watch (etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-yabai).
;;
;; NOT the watch itself. The watch is a deterministic hourly tick under
;; `tamaki exec` + LaunchAgent com.etzhayyim.yabai.ct-watch-tick (ADR-0004); it needs no
;; model and must not be recorded as if it had one. This loop is the judgement work AROUND
;; it — the tick can only catch brands that are in the roster, and there are five.
;;
;; Registering this spec does NOT start it: bin/tamaki-supervisor drives exactly one
;; TAMAKI_LOOP_SPEC. To activate:
;;   bin/tamaki loop ensure --spec loops/yabai-phishing-watch.edn
;;   bin/tamaki loop list
;;
;; Resolve :loop/project relative to TAMAKI_WORKSPACE / FLEET_ROOT / COM_JUNKAWASAKI_ROOT.
{:loop/id :yabai/phishing-watch
 :loop/enabled true
 :loop/description
 "Widen the worldwide brand-impersonation watch: grow the brand roster, add CT log shards,
  keep shared-infra ASNs accurate, and prove the murakumo fan-out. Never loosen the
  calibration — 36 benign domains must keep producing zero claims."
 :loop/tags #{:yabai :cti :phishing :coverage :continuous}
 :loop/objective
 "Raise what the CT watch can SEE, not what it claims. In priority order:
  (1) grow the brand roster beyond the five hand-written entries in phish-infra/default-brands,
      deriving candidates from evidence rather than taste, and re-run the benign/impersonation
      calibration sets after every change;
  (2) tail more CT log shards than argon2026h2 alone, refreshing ct-logs from the public
      log list as shards expire;
  (3) make the murakumo fan-out real — ct_watch --plan already produces a batch that
      `murakumo task plan --tasks` accepts, but running it needs the checkout present on the
      nodes;
  (4) keep shared-ip-asns correct as CDNs change, remembering that a wrong entry silently
      deletes a real signal.
  HARD invariant: test_phish_infra's benign set must keep producing zero claims and the
  impersonation set must keep being caught. A change that raises detection counts by
  loosening a threshold is a regression, not progress. Never send an abuse report."
 :loop/project "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-yabai"
 :loop/workspace-env "COM_JUNKAWASAKI_ROOT"
 :loop/continuous true
 :loop/interval-ms 3600000
 :loop/max-cycles 6
 :loop/max-failures 3
 :loop/auto-approve false
 :loop/organism-name "Yabai"
 :loop/runners ["codex" "claude" "grok"]}
